# OpenCLI automation (preferred)

For live browser / website automation, prefer **[OpenCLI](https://github.com/jackwener/OpenCLI)** over Cursor browser MCP, Selenium MCP, or ad-hoc Playwright scripts.

## When to use OpenCLI

| Goal | Skill to load first | Typical commands |
|------|---------------------|------------------|
| Orient / discover commands | `opencli-usage` | `opencli list`, `opencli doctor` |
| Drive logged-in Chrome (navigate, click, fill, extract) | `opencli-browser` | `opencli browser <session> …` |
| Use site sitemap while browsing | `opencli-browser-sitemap` | after `sitemap.available: true` |
| Write/update site sitemap knowledge | `opencli-sitemap-author` | after durable flows discovered |
| Author a reusable site adapter | `opencli-adapter-author` | recon → init → code → verify |
| Fix a broken `opencli <site> <cmd>` | `opencli-autofix` | trace → patch → retry |
| Search/query across sites via adapters | `smart-search` | adapter commands first |

## Agent workflow

1. Read the matching skill under `~/.cursor/skills/opencli-*` (or `~/.agents/skills/`).
2. Run `opencli doctor` before any `opencli browser *` or COOKIE/INTERCEPT/UI adapter work.
3. Prefer an existing adapter (`opencli <site> <command>`) over raw browser driving.
4. For ad-hoc UI: `opencli browser <session> open|bind` → `state`/`find` → act → re-`state` after navigations.
5. Always pass a `<session>` positional after `browser`. Close with `opencli browser <session> close` when done.
6. Prefer numeric refs from `state`/`find` over hand-written CSS; verify writes with `get value`.

## Do not replace with OpenCLI

- Formal Playwright E2E specs in this repo (`tests/**`, `pageObjects/**`, `Helpers/**`) — still use the UAE framework skills (`add-*-case`, `playwright-locator-expert`, etc.).
- OpenCLI may be used to **explore UI / confirm selectors** while authoring those tests; do not rewrite the test runner to OpenCLI unless the user asks.

## Prereqs (user machine)

- Node.js ≥ 20; `npm install -g @jackwener/opencli`
- Chrome + [OpenCLI Browser Bridge extension](https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/opencli/ildkmabpimmkaediidaifkhjpohdnifk)
- Skills installed via: `npx skills add jackwener/opencli -g -a cursor`
